 vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Talking About Social Occasions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Social occasions are times people get together for fun. Here are some common social occasions: <br><br>dinner party - people socialize when they eat dinner <br>birthday party - a celebration of a person's birthday <br>reception - the party after a wedding <br>anniversary - a celebration of a past wedding <br>baby shower - a party before you have a baby <br>housewarming - a party when you move to a new house<br><br> You can use modals (<span class=\"strong\">can</span>, <span class=\"strong\">could</span>, <span class=\"strong\">should</span>) to make a suggestion about a social occasion. See examples in the chart:", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modals\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Suggestion\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I can invite people to my house.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We could organize a birthday party.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"should\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We should have a baby shower for Heather.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "last minute", "type": "name"}, {"content": "organized very recently", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I know it's last minute, but we should do something! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le07ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to organize a social event.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to socialize", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to talk to people for pleasure", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Vanessa loves to socialize. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le07ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "wedding", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a ceremony uniting two people for life", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I promised to help my sister make wedding invitations.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le07ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "it doesn't give us much time ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "we don't have many days to plan", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That's in four days. It doesn't give us much time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le07ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "relative", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person you are connected to by family, but not in your immediate family", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I am having lunch with some relatives this afternoon.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le07ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "niece", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the daughter of your brother or sister", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm attending my niece's concert on Thursday.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le07ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "chips", "type": "name"}, {"content": "popular snack food made from potatoes", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We could pick up some chips, soda and cake for the party. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn3le07ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn3le07ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Choose a social occasion you attended, like a wedding reception or a party.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a list of 5 - 8 details about the event. Where was it? Who attended? What happened?", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Write 5 - 8 sentences about the event.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner, discuss how social occasions are different.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I identify a social occasion.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I describe the social occasion.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I compare ways to celebrate with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}]}